WEBVTT

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.677
Veruca.

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:13.680
Little girl?

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.559
( chattering )

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.894
Veruca, come back here at once.

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:24.190
Veruca!

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:28.528
( chattering )

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.536
WONKA:
Little girl?

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:39.164
Uh, don’t touch
that squirrel’s nuts.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.207
It’ll make him crazy.

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:53.761
( suspenseful melody plays )

00:00:57.682 --> 00:00:59.726
I’ll have you!

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:02.228
( squeals )
( gasps )

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.648
( squirrels squealing )
Veruca!

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.739
( gasping )

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:13.865
Veruca!

00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:16.910
( screaming )

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:22.707
Veruca!

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.750
( rattling )

00:01:23.791 --> 00:01:25.126
( screaming )

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.046
( whispers ):
If I could just find the key...

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.924
Nope, not that one.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.926
Daddy!

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.135
Veruca!

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:35.178
No.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.096
( chuckles )

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:39.891
( gasping )
( chattering )

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.026
Here it is.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:51.611
Here it isn’t.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:54.072
Daddy, I want them to stop!

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:57.116
( chattering stops )

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.079
( Veruca grunts )

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.540
( hollow thump )

00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:05.291
What are they doing?

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:08.294
They’re testing to see
if she’s a bad nut.

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:10.046
( high-pitched squawk )

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:10.922
Oh, my goodness.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.924
She is a bad nut, after all.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.467
( squirrels chattering )

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:15.760
( Veruca gasps )

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.474
MR. SALT:
Veruca!

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:23.351
Daddy!

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.811
Where are they taking her?

00:02:24.852 --> 00:02:27.313
Where all the other bad nuts
go-- to the garbage chute.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.482
( screaming )

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:30.483
Where does
the chute go?

00:02:30.525 --> 00:02:31.818
To the incinerator.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.862
But don’t worry.
We only light it on Tuesdays.

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:36.990
Today is Tuesday.

00:02:38.866 --> 00:02:40.493
Well, there’s always the chance

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:42.161
they decided not
to light it today.

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:43.663
( Veruca screams )

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:45.999
( gasping )

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:49.502
( nails scraping )
( squirrels chattering )

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:51.170
( screams )

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.715
Aah!

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:56.050
( yell echoes, stops )

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:02.307
Now, she may be stuck
in the chute

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.309
just below the top.
If that’s the case,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.228
all you have to do is just
reach in and pull her out.

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.689
Okay?

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.821
( creaking )

00:03:23.745 --> 00:03:25.455
( creaking )

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.206
( light pop intro begins )

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.084
♪ Ah, ah... ♪

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.379
♪ Ah-ah, ah-ah... ♪

00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:37.175
♪ Ah, ah... ♪

00:03:37.967 --> 00:03:40.762
♪ Ah-ah, ah-ah... ♪

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.848
♪ Ah, ah... ♪

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.101
♪ Ah, ah, ah... ♪

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:50.313
♪ Veruca Salt,
the little groot ♪

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:54.567
♪ Has just gone down
the garbage chute ♪

00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:58.029
♪ And she will meet,
as she descends ♪

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.240
♪ A rather different set
of friends ♪

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:04.952
♪ A rather
different set of friends ♪

00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:08.331
♪ A rather different set
of friends ♪

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.542
♪ A fish head,
for example, caught ♪

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.545
♪ This morning from a halibut ♪

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:18.007
♪ An oyster
from an oyster stew ♪

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:22.679
♪ A steak that no one else
would chew ♪

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:25.181
♪ And lots of other things,
as well ♪

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:32.230
♪ Which make
this rather horrid smell ♪

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:36.484
♪ Horrid smell ♪

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.278
♪ These are Veruca’s
new-found friends ♪

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.157
♪ That she will meet
as she descends ♪

00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:50.832
♪ These are Veruca’s
new-found friends ♪

00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:57.463
♪ Ah, ah, ah, ah... ♪

00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:00.299
♪ Ah, ah, ah ♪

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:04.137
♪ Ah, ah, ah... ♪

00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:07.765
♪ Ah... ♪

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:11.102
♪ Who would have spoiled her,
who, indeed? ♪

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:14.772
♪ Who bended
to her every need? ♪

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:18.109
♪ Who turned her into
such a brat? ♪

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:20.278
♪ Who was the culprit? ♪

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:21.738
♪ Who did that? ♪

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:25.491
♪ The guilty ones,
now this is sad ♪

00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:28.745
♪ Dear old Mum, and loving... ♪

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.954
( yells )
♪ Dad ♪

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.497
( scream echoing )

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:32.874
( stifled giggle )

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.252
( squirrels squeaking
in distance )

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.465
Really?

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.175
Oh, good.

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:44.969
I’ve just been informed that the
incinerator’s broken, so there

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.679
should be about three weeks
of rotten garbage

00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:47.680
to break their fall.

00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:50.433
Well, that’s good news.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.143
Yeah.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:53.603
Well...

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.354
let’s keep on truckin’.

00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:57.607
( bell dings,
doors rattle open )

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.859
I don’t know why I didn’t
think of this earlier.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:01.903
The elevator is by far
the most efficient way

00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:03.571
to get around the factory.

00:06:03.654 --> 00:06:05.656
There can’t be this many floors.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.451
How do you know,
Mr. Smartypants?

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.411
This isn’t just an ordinary
up-and-down elevator,

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:11.579
by the way.

00:06:11.662 --> 00:06:14.207
This elevator can go sideways,
longways, slantways,

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.708
and any other ways
you can think of.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.084
You just press any button...

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:19.212
( bell dings )
and, whoosh, you’re off.

00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:30.556
Oh, look! Look.

00:06:31.682 --> 00:06:33.059
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:06:33.142 --> 00:06:35.102
welcome to Fudge Mountain.

